#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:2
msgid "serial-port interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `serial-port` interface enables input and output access to a specific "
"serial port on a device typically running {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-"
"glossary_ubuntu-core>`. As a result, and because it provides such privileged "
"access to configure serial port hardware,  `serial-port` is considered a "
"restricted interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"Use  `snap interface serial-port` to see which serial-port devices are "
"available on the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"$ snap interface serial-port\n"
"name:    serial-port\n"
"summary: allows accessing a specific serial port\n"
"slots:\n"
"  - core:model01 (allows accessing a specific serial port)\n"
"  - core:monome (allows accessing a specific serial port)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:17
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via the path specified "
"by the connected slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:20
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:22
msgid "**Auto-Connect**: no</br> **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:22
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:81
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:24
msgid "Should specify a single path attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:25
msgid "`path` (slot): path to serial device node e.g. `/dev/ttyS1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:27
msgid "Or three attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"`usb-vendor` (slot): integer representing the USB Vendor ID, must be in "
"range 0 < vid <= 65535"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"`usb-product` (slot): integer representing the USB Product ID, must be in "
"range 0 <= vid <= 65535"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:30
msgid ""
"`path` (slot): path of the form `/dev/serial-port-...` where a symlink will "
"be created to the device e.g. `/dev/serial-port-mydevice`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"Hardware IO interfaces covers some general considerations common to these "
"kinds of devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:35
msgid ""
"To use a serial-port device, the snap developer must add `plugs: [ serial-"
"port ]` to a snap's [snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/"
"snapcraft/stable/reference/project-file/anatomy-of-snapcraft-yaml/). The "
"snap user can then access a specific serial-port device with an {ref}"
"`interface connection <explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:37
msgid "<h3 id='heading--code-examples'>Code examples</h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:39
msgid ""
"The following example shows the slot configuration, such as from the gadget "
"snap, and includes  which snaps are permitted to connect automatically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"serial-port:\n"
"    allow-auto-connection:\n"
"      -\n"
"        on-store:\n"
"          - (whatever)\n"
"        plug-names:\n"
"          - serial-foo\n"
"        plug-snap-id:\n"
"          - foooVbn5YriRw2sRVw7Cuj5PbjJjwnFb\n"
"        slot-attributes:\n"
"          path: /dev/whatever\n"
"        slot-names:\n"
"          - serial-foo\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:57
msgid ""
"All attributes must match for an auto-connection attempt to be successful. "
"The above example requires a connecting snap to have a matching snap-id and "
"plug name. For example, the following snapcraft.yaml stanza for the "
"connecting snap would _not_ connect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:59
msgid ""
"apps:\n"
"  whatever:\n"
"     plugs:\n"
"        serial-port\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:66
msgid ""
"While the following snapcraft.yaml stanza for the connecting snap would "
"automatically connect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:68
msgid ""
"apps:\n"
"  whatever:\n"
"     plugs:\n"
"        serial-foo\n"
"plugs:\n"
"   serial-foo:\n"
"      interface: serial-port\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:78
msgid ""
"The test code can be found in the snapd repository: [serial_port_test.go]"
"(https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/"
"serial_port_test.go)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/serial-port-interface.md:81
msgid ""
"The source code for the interface is in the snapd repository: "
"[serial_port.go](https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/"
"builtin/serial_port.go)</br>"
msgstr ""
